Make sure your virtual environment is activated (`source .venv/bin/activate`), then use the following commands:

---

### 1. Auto-format code (equivalent to Black)

```bash
ruff format .
```
This automatically rewrites files in the project to adhere to standard formatting conventions (indentation, quotes, line wrapping).

---

### 2. Check and auto-fix linting issues & import sorting (equivalent to Flake8 + isort)

```bash
ruff check --fix .
```
This finds lint issues (unused variables/imports, code smells) and automatically fixes everything it safely can, including sorting imports.

---

### 3. All-in-one check without modifying files (e.g. for CI/CD)

To see what would change or fail without writing changes:

```bash
# Check formatting only:
ruff format --check .

# Check linting only:
ruff check .
```

---

### Quick tip: Recommended one-liner

To format code and auto-fix lint issues in one step:

```bash
ruff check --fix . && ruff format .
```



